Hanumān surveys Nandana-like grove and thousand-pillared palace --- Hanumān spots fasting thin sighing Sītā ringed by Rākṣasīs --- Hanumān marks her single braid soiled sari and dimmed beauty --- Hanumān matches her worn jewels and fallen cloth to Rāma account --- Hanumān knows mutual love keeps Rāma and Sītā living --- Hanumān rejoices and praises Rāma in mind
